<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16562" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ex-alto</span></b> , āvi, ātum,
		1, v. a.
		altus (postAug.; mostly eccl. Lat.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To raise</i>, <i>elevate</i>, <i>exalt</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">deus alia exaltat, alia submittit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen.
					Q. N. 3</span></i>
			 prooem.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">TERMINOS VETVSTATE COLLAPSOS,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Fabr. p. 748</span></i>
			, <i>no.</i> 555: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">solium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Isa. 14, 13</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exaltare, Deus,</span>”
				<i>be praised</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Psa. 56, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vocem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Isa. 13, 2</span></i>
			 et saep.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To deepen</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fodiunt (sulcos) et exaltant in tres pedes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					3, 13, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sulcum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					3, 13, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">orbem ablaqueationis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 4,
					4, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
